Keep the detached input-popup focus listener as an empty list.

Firefox + Fcitx5 window teardown on Sway 1.12 can re-enter
input_popup_set_focus before a new surface is attached. Removing the
already detached listener then crashes in wl_list_remove.
Related upstream report: https://github.com/swaywm/sway/issues/8541
Retire this change when the packaged implementation keeps the listener
valid through teardown and the desktop application workflow passes.

--- a/sway/input/text_input.c
+++ b/sway/input/text_input.c
@@ -373,6 +373,7 @@
 static void input_popup_set_focus(struct sway_input_popup *popup,
 		struct wlr_surface *surface) {
 	wl_list_remove(&popup->focused_surface_unmap.link);
+	wl_list_init(&popup->focused_surface_unmap.link);
 
 	if (!popup->scene_tree) {
 		wl_list_init(&popup->focused_surface_unmap.link);
